+
+## Prizes (scoring, leaderboard, winners)
+- `quizzes.winners_count` ("Number of winners" in the quiz settings; integer 1..1000, default 3).
+  Read live from the quiz, so changing it after a game ends changes the "Top N" label.
+- Time: `games.question_opened_at` is set when a question opens; `answers.elapsed_ms` =
+  ms from that moment to the pick. A pick of a *different* option restarts it ("last pick");
+  re-sending the same option (retries) keeps the time.
+- `Game#leaderboard` → `Game::Standing(player, points, time_ms, place)`: points = correct
+  answers (option correctness is read at render time), ties → lower total time of correct
+  answers → earlier join. Places are 1..n (no shared places).
+- Winners: `players.winner`. `pick_top_winners!` / `draw_winners!` / `reset_winners!` (finished
+  games only, under `with_lock`, bump `state_version` + `broadcast_state`, so the screen and
+  phones update live). Only players with points are eligible. Draw: everyone above the N-th
+  place's points wins, the rest is `sample`d from players with exactly those points.
+  Routes: `POST /moderate/games/:id/top_winners|draw_winners|reset_winners` (no version check:
+  each "Draw" click draws again).
+- Big screen when finished: `ol.leaderboard > li.leader` (place, name + "Winner" badge,
+  "N points" + total time). Phone: "Place X of Y", "N points", "You won!". Points are never
+  shown before the game is finished.
+
+### Same-moment delivery
+- When a question opens, `broadcast_state` also carries the players' fragment (`html`,
+  rendered with `player: nil`; identical for everyone because nobody has answered yet), so
+  phones morph it in straight from the WebSocket without a round trip. Those forms have no
+  CSRF token; `player_controller#fixTokens` fills in the page's meta token and
+  `fetchWithTimeout` sends `X-CSRF-Token` on POSTs. Polls never morph an older version over a
+  newer one (`isNotOlder`).
+- The screen refreshes immediately on state pings (counter pings are still coalesced).
+- solid_cable `polling_interval` is 50 ms. Measured in production: phones show a new
+  question ~100–150 ms after the moderator's click.
+- Tests run with forgery protection off; the CSRF path was verified against `bin/serve`.
